hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27783","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyayna who said: Haddathani Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaa; he heard one of his family relate from his grandfather that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward the side of the door of Banu Sahm while the people were passing before him, and there was no sutra between him and the Kaba."
"27784","And Sufyan said another time: Haddathani Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaa from one who heard his grandfather say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward the side of the door of Banu Sahm while the people were passing before him, there being no sutra between him and the Kaba."
"27785","Sufyan said: And Ibn Jurayj had informed us from him, he said: Haddathana Kathir from his father, so I asked him, and he said: I did not hear it from my father, but from one of my family from my grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward the side of the door of Banu Sahm, there being no sutra between him and the circumambulation."
"27786","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Ibn Jurayj who said: Haddathani Kathir ibn Kathir from his father from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaa who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his week, come to the edge of the circumambulation and pray two rakas, with no one between him and the circumambulation."
"27787","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Khalid who said: Haddathana Rabah from Mamar from Ibn Tawus from Ikrima ibn Khalid from Jafar ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaa al-Sahmi from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Makkah Surat al-Najm and prostrated in it, and those with him prostrated; so I raised my head and refused to prostrate, and al-Muttalib had not embraced Islam that day; and he afterwards would not hear anyone recite it except that he prostrated."
"27788","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq who said: Haddathana Mamar from Ibn Tawus from Ikrima ibn Khalid from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaa who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in al-Najm, and the people prostrated with him; al-Muttalib said: And I did not prostrate with them, and he was that day a polytheist; al-Muttalib said: And I will never leave prostration in it ever."
